  "copy": {
    "series_title": "The Stories Behind the Trier Beer Festival 2026",
    "caption": "From Prüm in the Eifel to Trier: I’m featuring Prümer Brauhaus in The Stories Behind the Trier Beer Festival 2026.\n\nThe Brauhaus opened in Prüm in 2021, combining beer brewed on the premises with a restaurant centred on seasonal and regional cooking. That August, it hosted the Jazz-Initiative Eifel’s first Prümer Nachkirmes, a series of benefit concerts for people affected by severe weather. It was an early connection between the new brewpub and local cultural life.\n\nPrümer Brauhaus is joining the 12th Trier Beer Festival for the first time on 2–3 October 2026 at Blesius Garten, Trier, hosted by @kraft_braeu_trier and @blesius_garten.\n\nExplore the 2021 opening through the Beer Chronicles link in the accompanying Story.\n\nTickets are still available:\nhttps://www.ticket-regional.de/events_info.php?eventID=275224\n\n#BeerChronicles #TrierBeerFestival #PruemerBrauhaus #EifelBeer #BeerHistory",
    "story_text": "BEER CHRONICLES\nThe Stories Behind the Trier Beer Festival 2026\nPrümer Brauhaus logo\n2021\nA new brewpub opens in Prüm.\nTRIER BEER FESTIVAL · 2–3 OCTOBER 2026 · BLESIUS GARTEN\nTickets still available — see feed caption\nbeer-chronicles.org\n\nLink sticker: Explore their story\nhttps://beer-chronicles.org/?string=Pr%C3%BCmer+Brauhaus",
    "alt_text": "Warm cream editorial poster with centred charcoal serif text and fine copper rules. The heading reads “BEER CHRONICLES” and “The Stories Behind the Trier Beer Festival 2026”. The original Prümer Brauhaus logo is a wide green, beige, black and white wordmark. Below it are “2021” and “A new brewpub opens in Prüm.” The footer reads “TRIER BEER FESTIVAL · 2–3 OCTOBER 2026 · BLESIUS GARTEN” and “beer-chronicles.org”."
  },
